Mithila. King Janaka comes out on foot to meet them.
JANAKA: Sage, my house is honoured. And these two, who walk like lions and carry bows like grown men?
VISHVAMITRA: Sons of Dasharatha. They have come to see the bow.
JANAKA: Then they should hear how I came by my daughter. I was ploughing a field for a rite, and the blade turned up a child in the furrow. I named her Sita.
JANAKA: She will marry the man who can string the bow of Shiva. Kings have come. None could lift it.
>> prop cart bowCart at 0.56
It takes many men to drag it in: a long iron chest on eight wheels, and in it, the bow.
RAMA: May I touch it?
JANAKA: You may try.
>> move rama to 0.46 in 1
>> play greatBow \{\}
>> pose janaka raise
It breaks in the middle with a sound like a mountain splitting. Everyone but the king, the sage and the two princes falls to the ground.
JANAKA: I have seen it. I would not have believed it told. Sita is his.
JANAKA: Let riders go to Ayodhya tonight. Dasharatha must come to his son's wedding.
>> wash
